            <ArticleTitle>Relation between severity of disease and impairment of heart rate variability parameters in patients with chronic congestive heart failure secondary to coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>713-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The present data show that HR variability has a statistically significant, but moderate, correlation with clinical variables of severity of CHF. Therefore, HR variability analysis may be a new, important tool in the clinical assessment of CHF patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
